Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:35:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve fine ocean ripple detail with lossless WebP

---
 assets/ocean/README.md           |   6 ++++++
 assets/ocean/ocean-fine-256.webp | Bin 3078 -> 63458 bytes
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/assets/ocean/README.md b/assets/ocean/README.md
index 10f1411..687fcf0 100644
--- a/assets/ocean/README.md
+++ b/assets/ocean/README.md
@@ -23,3 +23,9 @@ Generated with built-in image generation on 2026-11-07. Original `exec-2877b59f-
 
 Exact prompt:
 Use case: photorealistic-natural. Asset type: original square seamless diffuse color texture for the open ocean in a real top-down Pacific aircraft game. Precisely vertical overhead view at moderate altitude, tightly cropped to a uniform patch of open deep Pacific seawater. Low-contrast dark navy-blue and subtle blue-green. Restrained natural wind-driven small capillary ripples and medium wavelets, with a faint irregular staggered rhythm and organic variation in directions. Most of the square is quiet dark water. The wave structures are shallow, short and irregular, not long parallel lines or broad folds. Gentle broken blue reflections describe the small waves without bright specular speckle. Approximately uniform color, value, and texture across the entire square, diffuse overcast light. This texture will be tiled and reduced to 256 pixels for a low-end phone. Maintain a small, consistent wave scale that remains legible when reduced. Seamless repeat at all four edges. No whitecaps, foam, wake, shoreline, boats, land, objects, horizon, cloud reflections, hotspot, spotlight, vignette, broad directional gradient, large waves, braided lines, fabric, crumpled paper, shiny plastic, typography, border, or grid.
+
+### Lossless encoding follow-up
+
+The same-source 256px Lanczos reduction now uses lossless WebP (`convert source.png -filter Lanczos -resize 256x256 -define webp:lossless=true ocean-fine-256.webp`). Runtime SHA-256 is `a5470bad2125f06000521533428b9575601384dbc8b7871496fb35e600a8ca0a`, and transfer size is 63,458 bytes. The dimensions, decoded texture format, wrapping, drift, cloud attenuation, and shader sampling are identical to the preceding trial.
+
+At aligned four-texel boundaries, the lossy decode's mean luma step measured 1.82× the all-adjacent mean horizontally and 1.15× vertically. Both ratios are 1.00× after lossless encoding, rounded to two decimal places. Across matching source texels, the lossy decode differed by 2.52 RGB byte values on average and up to 23. The prior CPU lighting comparison was for the lossy decode. The lossless encode recovers finer contrast, which still needs game-scale visual review.
